==Battleground==
*3 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*5 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 5.33~12 seconds<sup>160f~360f</sup>.
*5 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*5 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Easter Egg Cat (Enemy)|Easter Egg Cat]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Aku Doge]]s spawn, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
**4 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Using weak meatshields is not recommended as Easter Egg Cat's rapid Omni Strike attacks can wipe them out easily, instead pivot to strong tankers such as [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell Cat]]. Use Midrange and Backline units like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]] to defend and survive until all Aku Gories are defeated. After that, Easter Egg Cat can be slowly taken out with rushers, specifically [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]].

